  <h2 id="shadcn-interop">shadcn CLI Interop</h2>

  <p>
    The registry stays 100% shadcn-format, so the official <code>shadcn</code> CLI keeps working —
    useful in mixed teams or tooling that already speaks the protocol. Point it at our item URLs:
  </p>

  <code-block language="bash" code=INIT_CMD/>
  <code-block language="bash" code=ADD_CMD/>

  <p>Two details make this work for a non-React framework:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Every file ships as <code>"type": "registry:file"</code> with an explicit
      <code>target</code> path — the non-React path through shadcn's CLI, so it copies our
      <code>.marko</code> files verbatim instead of running React codemods over them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Every <code>registryDependencies</code> entry is an absolute URL into our registry. A bare
      name like <code>"utils"</code> would resolve against shadcn's own React registry.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="urls">Registry URLs</h2>

  <p>Every item is a static JSON file under the same base URL:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>URL</th>
        <th>What it is</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/registry.json</code></td>
        <td>The index — every item's name, type, and file list, without file contents.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/index.json</code></td>
        <td>The flat item array the marko-ui CLI reads for its interactive picker.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/registries.json</code></td>
        <td>The registry discovery index — entries declare <code>target: "marko"</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/&lt;component&gt;.json</code></td>
        <td>A single component, contents included. For example <code>/r/dialog.json</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/utils.json</code></td>
        <td>The <code>cn()</code> helper. Nearly every component depends on it.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/style.json</code></td>
        <td>The theme: <code>globals.css</code> plus <code>cssVars</code> for the CLI to merge.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/r/style-&lt;color&gt;.json</code></td>
        <td>The same theme in <code>zinc</code>, <code>slate</code>, <code>stone</code>, or <code>gray</code>.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>To list everything available:</p>

  <code-block language="bash" code=REGISTRY_INDEX/>
</docs-article>
